.TH ACC-CLI 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-cli \- operator command line for an ACC collective
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-cli
.RB [ \-v | \-vv ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ACTION ]
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-cli
is the one-shot operator interface to an ACC (Agentic Cell Corpus)
collective.
It surfaces every internal channel \(em the NATS bus, the LLM backend, the
role loader, the oversight queue, the session tracelog, the knowledge store
\(em through one command, so the same operations a TUI screen offers can be
scripted, run over SSH, or driven from CI.
.PP
Each command lives in its own module and imports its dependencies only when
it runs: a command that never touches the bus (\fBrole list\fR,
\fBconfig show\fR) works on a host where the collective is down.
Without a command,
.B acc-cli
prints its help and exits 0.
.PP
Most read commands accept
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
Commands that change governed state (oversight decisions, role infusion,
configuration, access) act as the principal
.B acc-cli access whoami
reports, and are subject to that principal's ceiling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase log verbosity: \fB\-v\fR for INFO, \fB\-vv\fR for DEBUG.
Logs go to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help for
.B acc-cli
or for any command or action and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
The commands below are generated from the parser of this release.
Every action also accepts
.BR \-h .
.\" @COMMANDS@
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACC_NATS_URL
NATS endpoint for every bus command (default \fBnats://localhost:4222\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID
Default collective for the bus and oversight commands (default \fBsol\-01\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_CONFIG_PATH
The \fBacc\-config.yaml\fR to read; otherwise found through the host layout
described in
.BR acc (1).
.TP
.BR ACC_ROLES_ROOT ", " ACC_SKILLS_ROOT ", " ACC_MCPS_ROOT
The role, skill and MCP trees; otherwise the share tree of the layout.
.TP
.BR ACC_HOME ", " ACC_SHARE ", " ACC_STATE
Override the configuration, data and state roots; see
.BR acc (1).
.TP
.B ACC_PACKAGES_ROOT
Where installed packages live (default \fB/var/lib/acc/packages\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/acc/acc\-config.yaml
The system configuration (an RPM install); \fI~/.config/acc/acc\-config.yaml\fR
for a per-user one.
.TP
.I /etc/acc/acc.env
Secrets for the stack, mode 0640 root:acc.
.B acc-cli secrets
and
.B acc-cli auth
report names only, never values.
.TP
.I ~/.config/acc/trust.yaml
Trusted workspace directories, managed by
.BR "acc-cli workspace" .
.TP
.I /var/lib/acc
Shared state: packages, instances, workspaces, sessions, trace.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero when the action failed or found a fault (for
example \fBdoctor\fR and \fBconfig check\fR exit non-zero on a finding);
130 when interrupted with Ctrl-C.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
acc\-cli doctor                       # deployment health, read-only
acc\-cli status                       # per-agent and collective health
acc\-cli role list
acc\-cli oversight pending
acc\-cli oversight approve <oversight_id>
acc\-cli nats sub 'acc.sol\-01.>'
acc\-cli trace <task_id> \-\-limit 100
acc\-cli config set \-\-dry\-run llm.backend openai_compat
acc\-cli collective diff               # spec vs. running containers
acc\-cli doctor \-\-paths              # where this host's ACC lives
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acc (1),
.BR acc-pkg (1),
.BR acc-tui (1),
.BR acc-deploy (1),
.BR acc-agent (1),
.BR acc-webgui (1)
